"[Linux/GTK] Fix file dialog accept behavior and mitigate keyjacking"
(crbugs 556516049, 562509446): the GTK file chooser's keyjacking
mitigation made Cancel the dialog's default response, and GTK accepts a
double-clicked file (or Enter in the file list) by activating the default
response, so those cancelled the dialog instead of choosing the file. The
fix restores the normal accept response and instead defers showing the
dialog until Enter and Space are released, and ignores accepts in its first
500 ms, as the Windows and Mac dialogs do. chromium/src main commit
35f55adbc49923b7508404d9a9a1fb7bc407a600 (2026-10-14), not merged to 157.
This is that commit, without its unit test. Drop it once a 157 tag has it.

